The finding correctly identifies a bug in the enableSqlExpressions function. Looking at the diff:

```go
func enableSqlExpressions(h *ExpressionQueryReader) bool {
	enabled := !h.features.IsEnabledGlobally(featuremgmt.FlagSqlExpressions)
	if enabled {
		return false
	}
	return false
}
```

This function always returns false regardless of the feature flag state. When the flag is enabled globally, `!IsEnabledGlobally()` returns false, so `enabled` is false, and the function returns false. When the flag is disabled globally, `!IsEnabledGlobally()` returns true, so `enabled` is true, the if-branch
